# ── Transport ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# "live" routes lib/api.ts through HTTP to Laravel. "mock" runs the in-browser
# fixture in lib/mock/ with no backend at all — useful for design work and for
# preview deployments that should not touch production data.
#
# In a live build the mock router and its dataset are tree-shaken out entirely,
# so this is a real switch and not a runtime branch.
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_MODE=live

# ── API base URL ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# MUST include the /api prefix: call sites pass paths like "/auth/login", and
# the base is concatenated with them as-is. A trailing slash is trimmed.
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8000/api

# ── Production (set these in the Vercel Production environment) ───────────────
# NEXT_PUBLIC_API_MODE=live
# NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=https://api.voucherflow.co.tz/api
#
# Both are NEXT_PUBLIC_*, so they are inlined at BUILD time. Changing them in
# Vercel does nothing until the next deployment rebuilds.
#
# lib/api.ts refuses to build a deployment that would not work: a missing URL
# in live mode, a relative URL, plain http to a real host, or — on a Vercel
# production build — a localhost address. Without that guard an unset variable
# silently falls back to 127.0.0.1 and every visitor's browser tries to reach
# its own machine.
